Translation patch: integer widenings in `value::convert::{chrono, time}`

Change: `year.into()` (`u16` to `i32`, chrono) and `days.into()`, `hours.into()`, `minutes.into()`, `seconds.into()`, `microseconds.into()` (`u8`/`u32` to `i64`, time) become `as` casts.
Why: These `From` impls between integer types are not modelled by Aeneas.
Behaviour: Identical: the conversions are lossless widenings, which `as` computes.

